       "reasons": [
        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/fz215xr4723.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "e1 carries a rubber stamp set diagonally across the paper, not writing: a heavy blotted mark with a tail, then a point, then four figures 4 1 [2 or 3] 8. The leading mark is the fixed blob reading.md warns about, so I have not counted it as a digit; the figures alone give 4.1.28. The third figure is clogged with ink and could as well be a 3, which would make it 4.1.38, so the year is the weak point. e4 carries the roll number 1443 in pencil, agreeing with the printed leader label in e5 (WELTE-MIGNON No. 1443, Sonata Appassionata Op. 57, 2nd and 3rd movements, Beethoven); e2, e3 and e6 are blank."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
